"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,625\nThe Learning Brain. Series 4: Habits\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,340\nEpisode 4\n\n3\n00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:09,714\nExercise and the brain\n\n4\n00:00:12,514 --> 00:00:15,011\nIf you have ever felt clearer after a walk,\n\n5\n00:00:15,253 --> 00:00:16,801\nyou are not imagining it.\n\n6\n00:00:17,290 --> 00:00:19,124\nMovement changes the brain,\n\n7\n00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:21,702\nboth over months and within minutes.\n\n8\n00:00:21,872 --> 00:00:25,669\nIn a year long trial with a hundred and twenty older adults,\n\n9\n00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:29,811\npeople who walked briskly three days a week grew their hippocampus,\n\n10\n00:00:30,057 --> 00:00:31,520\na key memory region,\n\n11\n00:00:31,803 --> 00:00:33,151\nby about two percent.\n\n12\n00:00:33,721 --> 00:00:36,709\nA stretching group lost about one and a half percent.\n\n13\n00:00:36,879 --> 00:00:39,519\nBut that study was in adults in their sixties,\n\n14\n00:00:39,609 --> 00:00:40,665\nnot students.\n\n15\n00:00:41,001 --> 00:00:42,479\nAnd on its memory test,\n\n16\n00:00:42,655 --> 00:00:45,417\nboth groups improved by similar amounts.\n\n17\n00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:47,982\nSo it shows the brain can change,\n\n18\n00:00:48,169 --> 00:00:50,981\nnot that a gym habit will raise your grades.\n\n19\n00:00:51,151 --> 00:00:52,668\nWhat about a single session?\n\n20\n00:00:53,177 --> 00:01:00,014\nA meta-analysis of seventy nine studies found a small boost to thinking during and after one bout of exercise.\n\n21\n00:01:00,478 --> 00:01:06,986\nA 2025 review of thirty meta-analyses put the average effect at small to medium,\n\n22\n00:01:07,434 --> 00:01:12,407\nand its authors suggest about twenty minutes at moderate to vigorous intensity.\n\n23\n00:01:12,577 --> 00:01:14,617\nFor memory, timing matters.\n\n24\n00:01:14,988 --> 00:01:19,181\nPooled studies found that exercise just before learning gave a small,\n\n25\n00:01:19,299 --> 00:01:20,532\nuncertain benefit.\n\n26\n00:01:21,026 --> 00:01:24,519\nExercise in the hours after learning gave a clearer one.\n\n27\n00:01:24,903 --> 00:01:27,680\nAnd exercising during learning tended to hurt.\n\n28\n00:01:28,264 --> 00:01:30,684\nVigorous exercise, and young adults,\n\n29\n00:01:30,891 --> 00:01:34,251\nshowed larger effects when the exercise came first.\n\n30\n00:01:34,421 --> 00:01:35,389\nSome caution.\n\n31\n00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:38,842\nEffects are modest and vary from study to study.\n\n32\n00:01:39,186 --> 00:01:42,160\nMany experiments are small and run in labs.\n\n33\n00:01:42,527 --> 00:01:44,853\nExercise will not replace studying,\n\n34\n00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:47,009\nbut it is a cheap way to support it.\n\n35\n00:01:47,179 --> 00:01:48,060\nTry this.\n\n36\n00:01:48,404 --> 00:01:52,081\nTake a brisk walk of ten to twenty minutes before a study session.\n\n37\n00:01:52,466 --> 00:01:53,643\nAfter a hard session,\n\n38\n00:01:53,663 --> 00:01:55,609\nmove again instead of scrolling.\n\n39\n00:01:56,019 --> 00:01:58,544\nDon't try to memorize while working out hard.\n\n40\n00:01:58,924 --> 00:02:00,948\nAnd build movement into every week,\n\n41\n00:02:01,085 --> 00:02:02,505\nnot just exam week.\n\n42\n00:02:02,675 --> 00:02:03,638\nMove your body.\n\n43\n00:02:03,649 --> 00:02:04,764\nHelp your brain.\n\n"
